{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Cancel Effects","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"sections":[],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every effect the store runs is already cancelled on teardown: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and the store’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cancel all in-flight effect tasks. That is enough for cleanup, but it is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"all-or-nothing","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — you cannot cancel one specific effect while others keep running.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keyed cancellation adds that. You give an effect a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"cancel id","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and later cancel every effect running under that id with the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" effect or the imperative ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" method. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" carries cancellation metadata alongside its async operation. The store registers declared cancellation scopes synchronously before starting background work, so an immediate cancellation cannot race registration.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reach for this when an effect outlives the action that started it: cancelling text-to-speech when the user skips, debouncing a search field, or tearing down a long-lived listener when a screen disappears.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Choosing an id","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Choosing-an-id"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A cancel id is any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value. Distinct ids are independent; effects sharing an id are cancelled together. A dedicated empty type reads well and can’t collide with another feature’s id:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["private struct SearchID: Hashable, Sendable {}","private struct SpeechID: Hashable, Sendable {}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Strings and enums work too — pick whatever is unambiguous in your domain.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Cancel from inside a reducer","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Cancel-from-inside-a-reducer"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Return ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to tag the work, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to stop it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["case .startSpeaking(let text):","    return cancellable(id: SpeechID()) { send in","        for await word in speech.speak(text) {","            await send(.spokeWord(word))","        }","    }","","case .skip:","    \/\/ Stop any in-flight speech immediately.","    return cancel(id: SpeechID())"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cancellation is cooperative: a stream or service must observe cancellation to stop its work. Keyed effects also suppress sends after cancellation, so a service that returns a stale successful result cannot publish it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Report the cancellation with `onCancel`","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Report-the-cancellation-with-onCancel"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Suppression covers ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"every","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" send after cancellation, including one from a ","type":"text"},{"code":"catch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block. A plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"Effect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can clear its own in-flight flag that way; a keyed one cannot, because the store can’t tell a cleanup action from a stale result. Name the cleanup action with ","type":"text"},{"code":"onCancel:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead, and the store dispatches it for you:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["case .search(let query):","    state.isSearching = true","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), onCancel: .searchCancelled) { send in","        await send(.results(try await api.search(query)))","    }","","case .searchCancelled:","    state.isSearching = false"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The store dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":"onCancel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" cancels the effect while it is still running — at once from view code, or right after the current action when a reducer returns ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". It is dispatched once, and never for an effect whose operation has already returned or thrown, even if the store has yet to forget it. An effect that is still running when the cancellation lands — even one that has just sent its result and is about to return — is cancelled, and reports it; a reducer that must not see ","type":"text"},{"code":".searchCancelled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" after ","type":"text"},{"code":".results","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" should ignore it there.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cancelling a scope cancels every scope nested in it, and each of those dispatches its own ","type":"text"},{"code":"onCancel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as well — outermost first — whether or not the enclosing scope has one. A nested scope often comes from another feature, and only its own ","type":"text"},{"code":"onCancel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" knows what that feature set.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"One case doesn’t dispatch it: a ","type":"text"},{"code":"cancelInFlight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" effect replacing this one. The action that started the replacement is already setting that state, and a late ","type":"text"},{"code":".searchCancelled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" would clear ","type":"text"},{"code":"isSearching","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" while the new search runs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Debounce with `cancelInFlight`","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Debounce-with-cancelInFlight"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Passing ","type":"text"},{"code":"cancelInFlight: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cancels any effect already running under the id ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" starting the new one — the whole of debounce in one line:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["case .queryChanged(let query):","    return cancellable(id: SearchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","        try await Task.sleep(for: .milliseconds(300))","        let results = try await api.search(query)","        await send(.results(results))","    }"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each keystroke re-dispatches ","type":"text"},{"code":".queryChanged","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the new effect cancels the previous sleeping one, so only the last query in a burst reaches the network.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Cancel from view or scene code","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Cancel-from-view-or-scene-code"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When there is no reducer action to hang the cancellation on — a screen disappearing, a sheet dismissing — call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" directly:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".onDisappear {","    store.cancel(id: SearchID())","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ids with nothing running are ignored, so it is always safe to call. No reducer runs here that could reset an in-flight flag, so give the effect an ","type":"text"},{"code":"onCancel:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" action if it sets one.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"What it does not replace","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"What-it-does-not-replace"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keyed cancellation is not a substitute for resource cleanup. An effect holding a file handle, a network connection, or an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncStream","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" continuation should still release it — use ","type":"text"},{"code":"withTaskCancellationHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or a ","type":"text"},{"code":"defer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Cancellation requests that the task stop; it does not close what the task opened.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Effects that terminate on their own (a ","type":"text"},{"code":"for await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" loop whose stream finishes) need no id at all. Only reach for a cancel id when something ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"else"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" has to stop the effect early.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Constructing and lifting effects","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Constructing-and-lifting-effects"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Create ordinary work with ","type":"text"},{"code":"Effect { send in ... }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". When a feature returns an effect with its own action type, lift it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["return featureEffect.map(AppAction.feature)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" preserves cancellation metadata. Wrapping another effect inside a new operation hides that declaration from the store until the inner effect is invoked. Such dynamically invoked scopes become active on invocation; cancelling an ID does not prohibit future scopes with that ID. Scope registrations are removed when their operation finishes, including when it throws. Cancellation keys are not retained as a history of past commands.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Nested scopes","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Nested-scopes"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A scope invoked inside another effect runs as its own child task, so cancelling its id cancels that scope alone. The effect hosting it carries on — the invocation throws ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which the host can catch — and so do the host’s other scopes, whatever their ids. That is what keeps a long-lived listener alive when one of the fetches it starts is abandoned:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["case .startListening:","    return Effect { send in","        for await event in events {","            let fetch: Effect<AppAction> = cancellable(id: FetchID(), cancelInFlight: true) { send in","                await send(.fetched(try await api.fetch(event)))","            }","            try? await fetch(send)  \/\/ `store.cancel(id: FetchID())` ends this fetch, not the loop","        }","    }"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cancelling the host still cancels every scope inside it. ","type":"text"},{"code":"cancelInFlight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on a nested scope replaces any other scope running under the same id, including a concurrent one in the same host (for example in a task group), but never a scope it is nested in.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects"},"abstract":[{"text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"How-to Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HostingRemoteConfig","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin"],"generated":true,"anchor":"How-to-Guides"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancelEffects()":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancelEffects"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancelEffects()","title":"cancelEffects()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancels all in-flight effects."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/canceleffects()","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"title":"Add a Version Killswitch","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that covers the UI of unsupported app versions, with an “Update” path back to the App Store."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddPersistence":{"title":"Add Persistence","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" macro — no hand-written "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" classes, database actors, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)":{"title":"cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tags an effect with a cancellation identity so it can later be cancelled by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.cancel(id:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancellable"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"kind":"text","text":" & "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"cancelInFlight"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":", ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Send","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux4Senda"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Void","preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Effect","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6EffectV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelinflight:_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddICloudSync":{"title":"Add iCloud Sync","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer opt-in, cross-device iCloud sync on top of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin — including a runtime opt-out toggle, launch-time entitlement detection, and the Apple Developer portal configuration."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddicloudsync","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAPaywall":{"title":"Add a Paywall","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"title":"Effect","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Async work with cancellation metadata declared before the store starts it."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/cancel(id:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/cancel(id:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancels every in-flight effect tagged with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" via"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancellable(id:cancelInFlight:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"cancel(id:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancel"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"},{"kind":"text","text":" & "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sendable"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/cancel(id:)","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HostingRemoteConfig":{"title":"Host Remote Config","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build the endpoint that serves killswitch and feature-flag config, so that it fails safe, can’t be cheaply exhausted, and passes a conformance checklist."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/hostingremoteconfig","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HostingRemoteConfig","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/cancel(id:)":{"title":"cancel(id:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancels scopes active when the store dispatches this effect, or when it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"invoked dynamically inside another effect. Undeclared future work is unaffected."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cancel"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"kind":"text","text":" & "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Effect","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux6EffectV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/cancel(id:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/cancel(id:)","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"title":"Swidux","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddFeatureFlags":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","title":"Add Feature Flags","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","role":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","title":"Add a Parental Gate"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"title":"Building a Domain Plugin","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"title":"Add Analytics","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxAnalytics"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","type":"topic"}}}